;; Written by Claude, 2026-10-14, for Phase 17 (design section 20,
;; proposal 8, approved by the user); reviewed by the user, 2026-10-14. It
;; replaces the file the user reviewed on 2026-10-14. Why this is right:
;; - Each of the 5 FOR loops ends before a step that would pass its
;;   final value (proposal 8), as on LLVM: after the body, SUBx3 at the
;;   variable's width computes the distance left (the final value less
;;   the variable counting up, the variable less the final value
;;   counting down), CMPx compares it with the step's size, and BGEQU
;;   goes on to the step, else JMP L^ leaves the loop. Each adds one
;;   label, so the labels after each are numbered one more.
;; The rest is as the user reviewed it on 2026-10-14:
;; - getEnv, when POC_TRNLNM finds no logical name (R0 negative), calls
;;   POC_GET_SYMBOL (.EXTERNAL), PocRtl's routine over LIB$GET_SYMBOL,
;;   with the name and returned; a negative length is FALSE, else val is
;;   emptied, that many characters of returned appended, and TRUE
;;   returned. A symbol defined empty is TRUE and "". POC_GET_SYMBOL's
;;   declaration and getEnv's longer comment and branch move every line
;;   number after them, the ones a trap passes (PUSHL #...) included.
;; The rest is as the user reviewed it on 2026-10-13:
;; - The table of open files, PLATFORM_TABLE_..., is 32 entries, each a
;;   768-byte control (PocRtl.mar's FAB, RAB, NAM block, XABFHC, XABDAT
;;   and resultant name), a 512-byte block, flags, the length, position
;;   and block start, and the record buffer's address and the current
;;   record's start and length. Entry 0 is StdIn's, opened on its first
;;   Read; 1 and 2 are never used, StdOut and StdErr going to LineOutput.
;; - Open finds the first free entry from 3 (else POC_STATUS(1),
;;   SS$_NOIOCHAN), calls POC_FILE_OPEN_MODE with the mode, and sets the
;;   entry from the three longwords it gives: a file read by block I/O
;;   has length (EBK - 1) * 512 + FFB; one read by record gets a 32767-
;;   byte buffer from POC_GET_MEMORY and is read through once by
;;   CountRecords, an LF counted after each record, then rewound.
;; - Read copies from the block LoadBlock brings in (writing the old one
;;   out first if dirty), never past the length; ReadRecords copies from
;;   the current record, an LF at its end, getting the next with
;;   POC_FILE_GET (-1 the end, 0 bytes then).
;; - Write to StdOut or StdErr gives each byte to LineOutput.Char, an LF
;;   to LineOutput.Ln; to a file, it is refused unless the entry is
;;   writable (POC_STATUS(2), RMS$_FAC), fills any gap past the end with
;;   zeros (Extend), then copies into blocks, marking them dirty and
;;   moving the length. WriteBlock writes min(512, length - block start)
;;   bytes, so that RMS keeps the file's end there.
;; - Truncate to a shorter length loads the block that holds the new
;;   end and writes it with POC_FILE_TRUNCATE, l - block start bytes
;;   (truncate-on-put); to a longer one, Extend.
;; - Identify calls POC_FILE_IDENTITY into the 32 bytes of FileIdentity;
;;   IdentifyByName opens the file with OldRO, identifies it and releases
;;   the entry. SameFile compares bytes 0-23 (device and file ID),
;;   SameFileTime 24-31 (the revision date); MTimeAsClock moves those 8
;;   bytes to a HUGEINT and takes it apart with POC_NUMTIM, as GetClock
;;   does POC_GET_TIME's.
;; - GetTimeOfDay subtracts 35067168000000000 (1 January 1970 as a VMS
;;   time) and divides by 10^7 for the seconds, and the remainder by 10
;;   for the microseconds (POC_HDIV, POC_HMOD); Time divides by 10^4
;;   since timeStart, modulo 7FFFFFFFH.
;; - System returns -1 when the command does not fit or POC_SPAWN fails,
;;   0 when the completion status is odd, else its low word (as a signed
;;   word, the CMPL with 32767 and SUBL2 of 65536).
;; - Chdir has POC_PARSE_DIRECTORY split the name into device and
;;   directory, defines SYS$DISK as the device (POC_DEFINE_DISK) and sets
;;   the directory (POC_SET_DIRECTORY), then makes CWD of the two.
;; - Fill refuses a name with no 0X in its array, as rtl/llvm does:
;;   GetEnv finds nothing, System returns -1, and a file procedure
;;   returns NameFailure's RMS$_FNF (POC_STATUS(4)), which Absent knows;
;;   a name too long for a service gets SS$_BADPARAM.
;; - The error tests call POC_STATUS_CLASS and test one bit each;
;;   ConnectionFailed and Interrupted return FALSE.
;; - Error returns lastError, which Result sets from every failing status.
;; - On the guest, vax-platform-files' PlatformFiles passes its 70
;;   checks under -O2 and -OC, and the default directory and SYS$DISK
;;   are as they were after it.
;; Compiled here in a program that contains Modules (Phase 17 step 3,
;; design section 19.5, proposals 2 to 4, approved by the user; written
;; by Claude 2026-10-13, reviewed by the user, 2026-10-13). It differs
;; from vax-files/expected-vax-Platform.mar only by the descriptor: the
;; .EXTERNAL POC_MODULE, the block "its descriptor, for Modules" (its
;; name, LineOutput imported, no commands), and the initializer's PUSHAL
;; L_MODULE_DESCRIPTOR and CALLS #1, G^POC_MODULE after its imports'
;; initializers.
;; Changed by Claude, 2026-10-13, for Phase 17 step 3 (design section
;; 19.11, proposal 2, approved by the user); reviewed by the user,
;; 2026-10-13. Platform now prompts for SYS$INPUT's records on a
;; terminal:
;; - promptInput, a new BOOLEAN in POC_DATA, is set in OpenInput before
;;   SYS$INPUT is opened: Fill("SYS$INPUT") and POC_IS_TERMINAL of it,
;;   then Fill("SYS$OUTPUT") and POC_IS_TERMINAL of that, each tested only
;;   if the one before was TRUE (&), the result MOVB'd to promptInput.
;;   OpenInput saves R2 now, which the & chain uses.
;; - NextRecord calls POC_INPUT_GET (a new .EXTERNAL), with the same three
;;   arguments as POC_FILE_GET, when k = StdIn (TSTL 4(AP)) and promptInput
;;   is set (BLBS); otherwise POC_FILE_GET as before. Both results go to n.
;; - The header comment says so, four lines longer, and promptInput is
;;   declared after table, so every later "; line" and trap line number is
;;   larger; and every label L_n after NextRecord's is renumbered. Nothing
;;   else differs: Platform's interface, and so its key, is unchanged.
;; - On the guest, vax-in, vax-in-extra and vax-instr read SYS$INPUT
;;   through it, a file there, by POC_FILE_GET; the prompt on a terminal
;;   was checked by hand.
;; Updated by Claude, 2026-10-15, for Phase 17 step 6 (design section
;; 22.3, proposal 6, approved by the user), for the user's review: CTRL/C
;; calls the interrupt handler, by the terminal driver's CTRL/C AST. New:
;; the variables commandChannel (a word) and interruptArmed (a byte); the
;; externals SYS$ASSIGN (five arguments, SYS$COMMAND by a CLASS_S
;; descriptor of length 11) and SYS$QIOW (all twelve, function 291,
;; IO$_SETMODE!IO$M_CTRLCAST, with P1 the AST routine's address or 0);
;; InterruptAst, which enables the AST again (MOVAB of its own address as
;; P1) and calls the handler with 2; ArmInterrupt, which assigns the
;; channel once and enables or disables the AST; and SetInterruptHandler
;; calling it when the handler's presence and the AST's state differ. So
;; the module's key (.IDENT), its line numbers and its labels after the
;; new procedures change; the rest is as reviewed before:
; Platform, written by poc (doc/developer/vax-macro32-backend.md)
	.TITLE	PLATFORM
	.IDENT	/2a203935c54e257b/
	.PSECT	POC_CODE,  PIC,SHR,NOWRT,EXE,LONG
